## Pre-Implementation: Repository Inspection

**Before writing code, inspect existing patterns in the same module.**

### Inspection Checklist

```
Before modifying backend/app/domain/inventory/:
  [ ] Check existing entity patterns (domain/inventory/entities/)
  [ ] Check existing repository interfaces (domain/inventory/interfaces/)
  [ ] Check existing handlers (application/inventory/handlers/)
  [ ] Check existing tests (tests/unit/domain/inventory/)
  [ ] Match existing naming conventions
  [ ] Match existing error handling patterns

Before modifying frontend/src/modules/sales/:
  [ ] Check existing component patterns (modules/sales/components/)
  [ ] Check existing hooks (modules/sales/hooks/)
  [ ] Check existing API service (modules/sales/services/)
  [ ] Check existing tests (modules/sales/__tests__/)
  [ ] Match component typing patterns
  [ ] Match state management patterns
```

### Anti-Pattern: Don't Assume Feature Missing

```python
# ❌ WRONG: Assuming material list doesn't exist
# Implement: list_materials()
# But it already exists in application/inventory/handlers/

# ✅ CORRECT: Check first
# grep -r "list_materials" backend/app/
# Find existing implementation
# Extend it instead of rewriting
```

