## 12-Step Implementation Workflow

### Step 1: Understand Requirement

**Read the full requirement. Document acceptance criteria.**

```
Example requirement:
"Add low-stock alert thresholds to materials"

Acceptance criteria:
1. Users can set reorder_point per material
2. Alert triggers when stock < reorder_point
3. Alert visible in inventory dashboard
4. RBAC: Only ADMIN, MANAGER can set threshold
5. Audit log all threshold changes
```

### Step 2: Inspect Existing Code

**Check if feature exists. Find similar patterns.**

```bash
# Check if material model has reorder_point
grep -r "reorder_point" backend/app/

# Check existing alert patterns
grep -r "Alert" backend/app/domain/

# Check existing thresholds/config patterns
grep -r "threshold" backend/app/
```

### Step 3-7: Plan Implementation

See `.cursor/rules/01-architecture.mdc` for layer structure.

### Step 8: Implement

Write code following patterns from existing modules.

### Step 9: Test

Run full test suite:

```bash
# Backend
pytest tests/ --cov=backend/app --cov-report=term-missing

# Frontend (from frontend/)
npm run test

# Type checking
pyright backend/app
npm run type-check

# Linting
ruff check backend/app
npm run lint
```

### Step 10: Verify Coverage

**Minimum 75% coverage for new code.**

```bash
pytest tests/ --cov=backend/app --cov-report=html
# Open htmlcov/index.html
```

