## 13-Point Definition of Done

**All items must be checked before claiming task complete.**

### 1. Requirement Met
- [ ] All acceptance criteria satisfied
- [ ] No criteria removed or partially satisfied
- [ ] Solution works end-to-end
- [ ] Edge cases handled

### 2. Architecture Validated
- [ ] DDD layers respected (domain → application → infrastructure → interfaces)
- [ ] CQRS pattern used (if applicable)
- [ ] No cross-layer coupling
- [ ] No circular dependencies

### 3. Business Rules Enforced
- [ ] Manufacturing rules checked (BOMs, WOs, inventory, etc.)
- [ ] Soft deletes respected
- [ ] State machines validated
- [ ] Domain exceptions raised for rule violations

### 4. Multi-Tenant Isolation
- [ ] Every query has `WHERE tenant_id = ...`
- [ ] Tenant from JWT, not request
- [ ] Test proves Tenant A cannot see Tenant B data
- [ ] Logs include tenant_id

### 5. Authorization Enforced
- [ ] RBAC check on endpoint (or middleware)
- [ ] 403 Forbidden on permission denied
- [ ] Permission denial logged
- [ ] Test: denied and allowed scenarios

### 6. Database Migrations
- [ ] Alembic migration created (if schema changed)
- [ ] Migration tested: `alembic upgrade head` works
- [ ] Downgrade tested: `alembic downgrade -1` works
- [ ] Indexes present on tenant_id, status, FKs

### 7. Tests Passing (≥75% Coverage)
- [ ] Unit tests written (domain logic)
- [ ] Integration tests written (repositories)
- [ ] E2E tests written (new endpoints)
- [ ] All tests passing: `pytest tests/`
- [ ] Frontend tests: `npm run test --run`
- [ ] Coverage ≥75% for new code

### 8. Frontend Components Typed
- [ ] No `any` types
- [ ] Props interface defined
- [ ] Return type explicit
- [ ] Error handling present
- [ ] Loading state handled
- [ ] Empty state handled
- [ ] Accessible (ARIA labels, keyboard nav)

### 9. Backend Code Quality
- [ ] Type hints on all functions
- [ ] Async/await for all I/O
- [ ] Structured logging with context
- [ ] Error handling explicit
- [ ] No hardcoded values/secrets
- [ ] No debug print statements

### 10. No Unrelated Changes
- [ ] Git diff contains only feature files
- [ ] No whitespace-only changes
- [ ] No unrelated refactoring
- [ ] No renaming unrelated code

### 11. Clean Commits
- [ ] Branch: `feature/TASK-ID` or `bugfix/ISSUE-ID`
- [ ] Commits: Atomic (one logical change each)
- [ ] Messages: Clear, include issue reference
- [ ] No force-push to main/develop

### 12. Limitations Documented
- [ ] Known issues noted (if any)
- [ ] Tech debt tracked (with TASK-ID)
- [ ] Temporary workarounds commented
- [ ] Future optimizations marked

### 13. Security Verified
- [ ] No secrets in logs
- [ ] No PII in logs
- [ ] Input validated (Pydantic)
- [ ] SQL injection prevented (parameterized queries)
- [ ] Passwords hashed (bcrypt 12+)
- [ ] CORS configured (not `*`)
- [ ] Rate limiting applied (if auth endpoint)

